## r03 (2026-10-21)

Grader bug F7 affected priority accuracy. Both numbers are shown. The regraded number is used for the verdict. The user still has to confirm that choice (D-r03-1).

| Metric | Config | Predicted | Measured | Same as last round | Verdict | Closer |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| priority_accuracy | C2 | 0.82 | 0.64 original / 0.79 regraded | 0.74 | Miss on original (off by 0.18). Hit on regraded (off by 0.03). | Prediction (0.03 off vs naive 0.05 off) |

Every other r03 config is regraded with the same script and logged in this same form. The original and regraded values come from `spe/evals/results/r03-regraded.json`.

### Which Why broke

No Why about the model broke for this row. The regraded 0.79 is within 0.05 of the 0.82 prediction. The broken assumption was in the harness. The selftest gate assumed trials would echo the exact casing of the key. That gap let F7 through, and the 0.64 shows it.

The naive guess (same as last round, 0.74) did not beat the prediction on the regraded number. On the original number, the naive guess was closer (0.10 off vs 0.18 off). That only happened because of the grader bug.
```

